  = help: usage: `g.instruments(exposure: Var, outcome: Var)`

error[Z0401]: `exposure:` of `instruments` is `x`, which is latent
 --> scripts/main.zeff:5:25
  |
5 | g.instruments(exposure: x, outcome: y)
  |                         ^ declared `latent` in the graph
  |
  = help: a model by instrumental variables needs the exposure and the outcome in the data; if `x` is measured after all, take it out of the `latent` line

error[Z0401]: `outcome:` of `instruments` is `y`, which is one the data are selected on
 --> scripts/main.zeff:5:37
  |
5 | g.instruments(exposure: x, outcome: y)
  |                                     ^ declared `selected` in the graph
  |
  = help: the data hold `y` fixed, so they show no relation of it to anything; if `y` varies in the data, take it out of the `selected` line

error[Z0401]: `exposure` of `instruments` must be a Var, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:25
  |
2 | g.instruments(exposure: "x", outcome: y)
  |                         ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: name one node of the graph, without quotes

error[Z0404]: `instruments` has no argument called `type`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:40
  |
2 | g.instruments(exposure: x, outcome: y, type: all)
  |                                        ^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `g.instruments(exposure: Var, outcome: Var)`

error[Z0401]: `instruments` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | dataset(wages).instruments(exposure: educ, outcome: wage)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `instruments` takes a Dag first; `x.instruments(...)` is `instruments(x, ...)`

